@Mean Old Lady
LLM = Large Language Model, the technical name for the central mechanism of Al (may its talons crumble). Al scrapes up and swallows immense amounts of language samples AKA texts (hence, LLMs) and then analyses the sludge of words by taking, say, the word 'helter' in a text identified as English and counting how many times it's followed by the word '-skelter' (almost always) and how often by 'begonia' (never). 
It then 'concludes' (reminder: it's a machine, it doesn't think) that 'helter-skelter' is an English phrase that English readers will expect and understand. It does this 10^? times, forms gazillions of associations and presents these word associations as 'thought.'

